# Distributed Web Infrastructure

## Infrastructure Diagram
https://github.com/ixhadeel/holbertonschool-system_engineering-devops/blob/main/web_infrastructure_design/1-distributed_web_infrastructure.png

## Components
- HAProxy distributes incoming traffic between two application servers.
- Round Robin sends requests to each server in rotation.
- Both application servers are Active-Active and handle requests simultaneously.
- Active-Passive means one server handles traffic while another remains on standby.
- Each application server contains Nginx, an application server, application files, and MySQL.
- MySQL Primary handles writes and replicates data to MySQL Replica.
- MySQL Replica handles read queries.
- Both application servers send database writes to the Primary.

## Infrastructure Issues
- SPOF: The single HAProxy load balancer.
- SPOF: The MySQL Primary for write operations without automatic failover.
- Security: No firewall and no HTTPS.
- Monitoring: No monitoring system is configured.
